\f0\b \cf0 (2 Billion years Before The Dawkins)
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 Two billion years before the birth of the saviour, around the time the earth was a molten, glowing pock marked teenager, two super giant singularities, gravitationally love locked in an irresistible cosmic ballet, dragged their galaxies away out onto a rippling time-space dance floor. They banked in elliptical flight paths, curving majestically through the cosmos on their billion year courtship. The spiral arms formed up in protective ranks as the singularities hurtled towards one another, drawn at unimaginable speed, accelerating exponentially as they closed in. Millions of elderly blue giants, middle aged red dwarfs and yellow upstarts smashed into one another, clearing a path for their parent black hole, but the shy couple only pecked each other on the cheek in a glancing blow at near light speed and gracefully pirouetting under the gaze of a hundred billion fabulously lit celestial balls. Giant tentacles and slender tendrils of shimmering stars reached out to seize the gravity wells, whipping space-time in frustration as the singularity slipped through their grasp. Showers of stars, stellar debris and dust clouds shot out in every direction, flushing the universe with radiation and explosions of magnitudes immeasurable.
\f1 \

\f2  The anticipation of becoming one in an eternal embrace of pure bliss, spun them in gleeful celebration as they turned, once again hurtling toward one another, ever faster, in diminishing orbits. Racing around one another at impossible speeds the smitten pair became ravenous and snacked upon solar systems, neutron stars and constellations. As the cadence of the dance increased, the irresistible urge to consume and destroy overwhelmed and they gorged on nebulae and star clusters, ripping away massive chunks of entire galaxies. Stars lined themselves up in giant gleaming white lines that were veraciously snorted by the spinning, dark lovers in a coke fueled fuck-frenzy, impossible to stop. Time twisted and tangled around itself, mangling into massive, unseen, Gordian knots held fast by gravity, last week strangling next year.
\f1 \

\f2 Observing with disdain from beyond the merging event horizons, a much maligned and misunderstood diffuse galaxy charged in uninvited. Although, more vast than most galaxies, it did not comprise of a central black hole and to his galactic peers he was a low emitting light weight, deserving only scorn and derision. Comprised almost entirely of concentrated dark matter, the fluffy galaxy daintily crossed the event horizon unnoticed and cut in between the two singularities in an audacious astral cock-block, but the two points of infinite density touched, simultaneously penetrating and engulfing each other in an androgynous union of trans-dimensional perfection. 
\f1 \

\f2 The introduction of a highly concentrated dark matter, the stellar equivalent of a timely finger in the arse, turbo charged the explosion of joy, sending not a ripple, but a tsunami of gravity waves across the universe, dangerously distorting space-time. 
\f1 \

\f3 \
